,title,link,text,language,family
0,Mayangna people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayangna_people,"The evidence provided by an analysis of the Misumalpan language family, to which the Mayangna languages belong and which also includes Miskito and the extinct Matagalpan and Cacaopera tongues once spoken in the Nicaraguan highlands and southern El Salvador, indicates the continuous presence of these groups in the region from around 2000BC. [5] In fact, until the migration from southern Mexico ...",Mayangna,Misumalpan
1,Misumalpan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misumalpan_languages,"The Misumalpan languages (also Misumalpa or Misuluan) are a small family of languages spoken by different Indigenous groups in the region commonly known as Mosquitia, referred to in Miskitu as Yapti Tasba Masrka (""the People's Land"").",Mayangna,Misumalpan
