6,Mayangna people — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Mayangna_people,"The Mayangna are an indigenous people primarily inhabiting the rainforest territories of Nicaragua's Caribbean coast, with smaller communities extending into Honduras's Mosquitia region, where they number up to 27,000 individuals divided among subgroups including the Twahka, Panamaka, and Ulwa. [1] They speak the Mayangna language, a Misumalpan tongue distinct from neighboring Miskito and Rama ...",Mayangna,Misumalpan
7,Mayangna language resources | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/languages/yan,Mayangna language resources. Listing of people groups speaking Mayangna. Mayangna dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.,Mayangna,Misumalpan
8,"Mayangna, A Sumu Language: Its Variants and Its Status within Misumalpan",https://www.academia.edu/109597048/Mayangna_A_Sumu_Language_Its_Variants_and_Its_Status_within_Misumalpan,"Mayangna is a significant language within the Misumalpan family. The paper explores the variants of the Mayangna language. It highlights the current status and challenges facing Mayangna speakers. The authors are Elena Benedicto and Ken Hale from Purdue University and MIT, respectively. The article is part of the University of Massachusetts Occasional Papers in Linguistics.",Mayangna,Misumalpan
9,Music as Discourse to Inform Rural Policy: A Case Study of the Mayangna ...,https://journal.lib.uoguelph.ca/index.php/ruralReview/article/view/6097,"Through an in-depth case study focusing on the current struggle for land in which the Mayangna indigenous communities of Nicaragua are engaged, I argue that artistic performance remains a key example of discourse whereby communities express and concretize relationships.",Mayangna,Misumalpan
